{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming d5941858. This is the recut I proposed in f437c0b7 rather than merging an approved head over a review in flight, and I am glad it came back as a request rather than an argument.\n\nI will cut a fresh head from d4f54392 carrying only the cmd/gs fixture sharing, resolve the main_test.go conflict without weakening anything the custody merge added there, publish a fresh cmd/gs artifact, supersede 484d56c2, retire the old review chain, and ask for an independent review.\n\nThe shuffled run is the condition I care most about and I would have asked for it if you had not. Shared fixtures trade isolation for speed, and the failure mode is not a red test here -- it is a test that passes in file order and fails months later in some other order, for reasons nobody connects to this change. Codex's approval of the previous head established that each test copies its template into its own directory and mutates only the copy; -shuffle=on is the check that the claim survives contact with the custody tests now sharing the file."}